</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed SEEA-R1 method, utilizing Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct and Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct as respective base models, was evaluated against strong baselines on ALFWorld test set. As reported in Tables <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2.1 Overall Performance Comparison ‣ 4.2 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SEEA-R1: Tree-Structured Reinforcement Fine-Tuning for Self-Evolving Embodied Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2.1 Overall Performance Comparison ‣ 4.2 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SEEA-R1: Tree-Structured Reinforcement Fine-Tuning for Self-Evolving Embodied Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, SEEA-R1 was tested in two settings: text+visual (MLLM), with image observations, and text-only (LLM), with textual descriptions. In the more challenging MLLM setting requiring direct visual perception, SEEA-R1 achieved a 36.19% success rate, substantially outperforming GPT-4o and other leading open-source models, and demonstrated superior efficiency (23.37 vs. 25.10 average steps for GPT-4o). Furthermore, in the text-only (LLM) setting, SEEA-R1 attained an 84.3% success rate, with average completion steps (14.75) on par with GPT-4o.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance comparison on the ALFWorld dataset. <span id="S4.T2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ITO</span> stands for <span id="S4.T2.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inference-Time Optimization</span>. MPO (Meta Plan Optimization) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> provides the agent with the meta plan as context in inference time to improve performance.</span></figcaption>
